I made two fixes in `episodes/horror-building-intercom-buzzes-3-m/shots.json`, and `--check` prints PASS. I didn't re-render the stills, so neither fix has been checked visually.

- **Scene 12, peephole (stills at 55.43 and 58.0 s):** both frames were nearly black. I raised Peephole `exposure` from 1.2 to 2.2, softened its `vignette` to 0.45 and turned `flicker` down from 0.4 to 0.25, so the empty hall should now show.
- **Scene 13, end card (stills at 70.99 and 72.61 s):** the text "Your spare key is still on the hook inside my door." ran past the bottom of the red card and sat under the PART 2 stamp. I shortened it to "YOUR KEY NEVER LEFT." and moved the stamp down (`stampY` from 0.6 to 0.74). This changes the wording of the final card.

One thing I left as it is: at 32.47 s, the zoomed chat pushes the top bubble under the caption "is at the front door." It's still readable, but you can see the overlap.
